From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] wificond: signal strength without the failed-packet count

Test V34: Wi-Fi is connected and in use, but the framework has no signal
strength for it - "RSSI: -127, Link speed: -1Mbps", mLastSignalLevel -1, the
Wi-Fi icons show an empty fan - and logs every three seconds

  wificond: Failed to get NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_FAILED
  WificondControl: Invalid signal poll result from wificond

NetlinkUtils::GetStationInfo() gives up on the whole reply when the count of
failed transmissions is missing. cfg80211 reports that count since Linux 3.2;
the PW3 kernel is 3.0. Signal strength, bit rate and the count of sent packets
are in the reply. A missing count is taken as none failed.

--- a/net/netlink_utils.cpp
+++ b/net/netlink_utils.cpp
@@ -370,8 +370,9 @@
     return false;
   }
   if (!sta_info.GetAttributeValue(NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_FAILED, &tx_bad)) {
-    LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to get NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_FAILED";
-    return false;
+    // Reported by cfg80211 since Linux 3.2 only. Not a reason to withhold
+    // the signal strength and the bit rate that are in the same reply.
+    tx_bad = 0;
   }
   int8_t current_rssi;
   if (!sta_info.GetAttributeValue(NL80211_STA_INFO_SIGNAL, &current_rssi)) {
